  "notes": "Block-13 cause field literally contains ';' in source data — mapped to cause_code TBD/provisional since no coded cause letter was actually provided (form gave cause_code TBD, category provisional, matching this). The event is a security/safeguards LER, not a plant equipment failure; I/O Board loss-of-communication alarms are the triggering equipment condition but the reportable failure is the human/procedural lapse in establishing a compensatory measure. A separate, unaddressed condition report investigates the I/O board hardware failures themselves — not modeled here since narrative explicitly excludes it from this LER's scope. No previous similar occurrence was found (explicitly stated none in 2019-2021), so no SIMILAR_TO stub LER emitted. No manufacturer given for the relay/board components beyond the RLY code itself, so no Manufacturer node emitted (RLY appears to be a component-type code, not a manufacturer code, per EIIS convention 'Security System [IA] - Relay [RLY]')."
